---
alwaysApply: true
---
- This application spoofs the coordinates of a mobile phone from a computer using the binary / executable ADB
- All things related to GUI are in `src/gui`.
- Reusable GUI components are in `src/gui/components/` (import via `gui.components`; `src/gui/elements.py` is a compatibility shim).
- All things related to model are in `src/core`.
- All things related to Leaflet map are in `src/geo`.
- Communication between the graphical interface and the model is done through the controller `src/controller`. 
- The graphical user interface is developed using the PySide6 package.
- Algorithmic logic must be commented on as much as possible.
- Communication between computer and phone is done using Android Debug Bridge in `src/assets`
- Project has a conda environment (AROW), before running shell command, add a `conda activate AROW`
